  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Phlegmanol C may interact with PITSLRE serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L2 through multiple indirect pathways. The drug Phlegmanol C is shown to target T-24, which is a target of Diosmetin-7-O-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->2)-6-O-Acetyl-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->2)-[Alpha-Lrhamnopyranosyl-(1->6)]-Beta-D-Glucopyranoside, and also of Yesanchinoside J, which further targets CDC2L2. Additionally, Phlegmanol C is linked to a compound that targets a benzene derivative, which in turn targets CDC2L2. These findings collectively indicate that Phlegmanol C may influence the activity of CDC2L2 through different molecular mechanisms, possibly involving the activation or inhibition of serine/threonine protein kinases. The evidence is supported by multiple high-scoring pathways, suggesting a potential role for Phlegmanol C in modulating CDC2L2 activity, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
